@startuml testing
title Testing View - automation pyramid (480 tests total)
caption Wider base = more, faster, cheaper tests. Counts and % are measured; 273 + 119 + 88 = 480.

skinparam defaultFontName Segoe UI
skinparam rectangle {
  BorderColor #566573
  BackgroundColor<<a>> #F7D6D6
  BackgroundColor<<i>> #F7E9C6
  BackgroundColor<<u>> #CFE8CF
}

rectangle "AcceptanceTests (full-system, Playwright)\n88 tests - 18%\ndrives running Blazor app + MCP-over-HTTP + rate limiting" <<a>> as A
rectangle "IntegrationTests (real EF Core + SQL Server)\n119 tests - 25%\nMediatR handlers, StateCommandHandler, mappings, gRPC, WebSocket\n" <<i>> as I
rectangle "UnitTests (NUnit/Shouldly/AutoBogus + bUnit)\n273 tests - 57%\n(~34 are in-memory WebApplicationFactory/bUnit - really integration)\n\n" <<u>> as U

A -[hidden]down- I
I -[hidden]down- U

note right of A
  Slowest, most expensive per test.
  Runs before every PR
  (acceptancetests.ps1).
end note
note right of I
  Coverage GAPS (no test):
  Forecast/Attachment query handlers,
  12 Core validators (direct),
  RealtimeNotificationHub, gRPC service,
  several controllers + health checks.
end note
note right of U
  Shape: broadly healthy pyramid.
  Caveat: unit base softened by
  ~34 web/component tests filed as unit.
  Coverlet wired; no coverage gate.
end note

legend bottom
|= Color |= Pyramid level |= Speed / cost |
|<#F7D6D6> | Acceptance (top) | minutes each - costly |
|<#F7E9C6> | Integration (middle) | seconds each |
|<#CFE8CF> | Unit (base) | milliseconds each - cheap |
endlegend
@enduml
